From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:59:08 +0000
Subject: iommu/arm-smmu-v3: disable PRI on the Sky1 PCIe SMMU

Sky1's IORT reports ATS, but not PRI, for the PCIe root complex.
Enabling the MMU-700 PRI queue on this integration produces sustained
C_BAD_STREAMID events (~130 IRQ/s on CPU0) followed by PCIe transaction
failures; the working vendor 7.0 configuration never enables
CR0.PRIQEN.

Mask ARM_SMMU_FEAT_PRI for the Sky1 PCIe SMMU before the in-memory
structures are initialised, so a generic configuration with
CONFIG_PCI_PRI=y ends up in the same hardware state: no PRI queue
allocated and PRIQEN never set.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
index a33b434d6..25bda609a 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
@@ -5639,6 +5639,20 @@ static int arm_smmu_device_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Sky1's IORT reports ATS, but not PRI, for the PCIe root complex.
+	 * Enabling the MMU-700 PRI queue on this integration produces
+	 * sustained C_BAD_STREAMID events followed by PCIe transaction
+	 * failures. Mask PRI before queue allocation so a generic
+	 * configuration with CONFIG_PCI_PRI=y ends up in the same hardware
+	 * state (no PRI queue, PRIQEN never set).
+	 */
+	if (arm_smmu_is_cix_sky1_pcie(smmu) &&
+	    (smmu->features & ARM_SMMU_FEAT_PRI)) {
+		smmu->features &= ~ARM_SMMU_FEAT_PRI;
+		dev_info(dev, "CIX Sky1 PCIe SMMU: PRI disabled\n");
+	}
+
 	/* Initialise in-memory data structures */
 	ret = arm_smmu_init_structures(smmu);
 	if (ret)
-- 
